# Suite-tier verify budget (#1509, folded in from #1041).
#
# The wall clock the driver gives the SUITE tier — `.pi/verify-cmd` in each
# worktree, its consolidated run, and the baseline probe that re-runs the same
# command at the cycle's base commit. First non-empty, non-comment line, a
# positive number of milliseconds, read like every other `.pi/` config file.
#
# Why a file and not only the env var (#1041): PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_MS
# belongs to the Pi process, so a project whose gate legitimately needs longer
# than the default could not say so itself — every operator had to export a
# variable before launching. This repo's full offline suite is ~641 files; at
# 2 jobs under load it measured past the old shared 10-minute bound, which
# parked healthy cycles at `verify-failed:develop` on code that was never
# judged. 30 minutes is the documented suite-tier default
# (`PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_SUITE_TIMEOUT_MS`), stated here explicitly so the gate's
# budget is visible next to the command it bounds rather than being an ambient
# number somebody remembers.
#
# Precedence (highest first): PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_SUITE_TIMEOUT_MS →
# PI_ENSEMBLE_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_MS → this file → the documented default.
# Fast tier: .pi/verify-cmd-fast-timeout-ms. Smoke tier: .pi/smoke-cmd-timeout-ms.
# An unparseable value (non-numeric, zero, negative) is ignored with a trace and
# the next level answers; `0` in particular never reaches exec, which reads a
# zero timeout as "no bound at all".
#
# `.pi/` is a protected path, so an unattended /work cycle cannot rewrite these
# budgets — same rule as .pi/verify-cmd.
1800000
